Added `identities`, `source` and `profile_url` to what `@users` says about a user. An administrator looking at an account could see its roles and its groups but not the one thing this package exists for — which external identities it is reachable through, and whether the account came from Plone's own user folder at all.

`source` names the PAS plugin the userid came from, and is read rather than derived: `searchUsers` aggregates the registered enumeration plugins and stamps `pluginid` on the record it returns, so this reports the plugin PAS itself resolved to instead of re-running the resolution and hoping to agree. `exact_match=True` is doing real work there — `searchUsers(id=...)` is a substring search, so without it a question about `alice` would be answered about `alice2`.

`identities` lists the provider, subject and timestamps of each link, and nothing else: the claims stored against an identity stay where they are. `profile_url` points at the user's Profile when the `[profile]` layer is installed and first login has minted one, and is `null` otherwise — including on a site where the extra was never installed, which is the case a serializer that assumed the layer would have failed on. @ericof
